hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1194","Abu Omar Hafs bin Amr Al-Rubali told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Israel bin Yunus told me, on the authority of Maysarah bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, “He prayed Maghrib with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he prayed until he prayed \Dinner\"""""
"1195","Abu Bakr said: It was narrated by Omar bin Abi Khath’am Al-Yamimi, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abi Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays six rak’ahs after sunset does not speak anything between them except in the remembrance of God.” “They were equal to Him by worshiping Him for twelve years.” Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Khath’am Al-Yamami, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, h. And Hafs bin Amr Al-Rubali narrated to him, on the authority of Zayd bin Al-Hubab, Omar bin Abi Khath’am Al-Yamimi informed me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, without Al-Rubali said: He should not speak ill between them."
